        <briefdescription>
<para>Reads a raw environment variable. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Asks the operating system for the value stored under <computeroutput>key</computeroutput>. In plain words: &quot;is there a variable with this name, and if so what text
does it hold?&quot; The answer is wrapped in an optional so that &quot;not set&quot; is clearly different from &quot;set to empty text&quot;. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">key</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Variable name. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The value as a string, or std::nullopt when the variable is not set. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
