    <briefdescription>
<para>Thin protected wrapper around the process environment (getenv/setenv). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Provides the raw accessors on which <ref refid="classEnvLoader" kindref="compound">EnvLoader</ref> builds its typed conversions. The helpers are static and protected so only derived configuration types (or test code deriving from them) can read or modify the environment; callers are expected to use the <ref refid="classEnvLoader" kindref="compound">EnvLoader</ref> overloads instead.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>The set of environment variables is process-global. Reading is safe while no other thread mutates the environment; mutation is intended for setup/test code before threads start, not for the request path. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classEnvLoader" kindref="compound">EnvLoader</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
